 In this image, we see ATAC peaks, gene expression, and a loop. ATAC data shows how accessable chromatin is in a certain area of the genome. The peaks we see are regions of open and accessable chromatin in the genome. These open stretches of chromatin are were regulatory elemnts bind to activate or inactivate genes, thus playing an important part in gene regulation. 

The RNA data or coding elements are used to measure gene expression. These are not regulatory elements but rather coding parts of the gene, measured by amount of mRNA transcripts.

Loops physically fold the genome, bringing different elements like promotors and enhancers closer together. All of these elements play a part in showing how different areas of the genome work together to regulate and control gene expression.